backlog-the-day-start-runs-domain-top-needs-a-build-with-more-vertical-levels-and-the-daytime-aegl1-fall-is-unexplained EXIT=0 :: Created Issue: aeef615f-9465-4cb2-8063-7b195182c2c4
  name: backlog-the-day-start-runs-domain-top-needs-a-build-with-more-vertical-levels-and-the-daytime-aegl1-fall-is-unexplained
  description: Future work (HB-196 ADDENDUM-03 item 5; HB-192 ADDENDUM-02 item 6; docs/evidence/hb192/vertical_top.md, tops_i81_day.tsv): the engine's own daytime mixed layer on i81-md-pa-line-day is 1,035 and 1,100 m, four times the 250 m domain top a day-start brief runs at, so the shipped run holds no mass above 250 m by construction. A taller top cannot be run at the 1.25 m vertical setting in this build: the number of levels is min(ZMAX/VRES, 200) (set_grid.f90, MAXGZ 200), so past 250 m the cell coarsens (2.5 m at 500 m, 5 m at 1,000 m), and those runs shrink the AEGL-1 area further (17.22, 16.40, 15.80 km2) rather than restoring it. So the 250 m top does not explain the fall of the daytime AEGL-1 area between the 250 m and the 1.25 m settings, and that fall is unexplained. Proposed, not run: the same measurement in a models-image build with MAXGZ raised to 1,000, so the top can rise at 1.25 m. Related: Issue c21aae38 (a day-start brief's SLAB check reads its daytime class).
  type: missing_content
  quadrant: BACKLOG (importance=medium, urgency=low)
  detection: review
  target: code
  state: open
