  name: limit-the-moving-clouds-status-line-mid-run-is-seen-only-in-a-live-run
  description: Known limit (HB-196 ADDENDUM-03 item 5; HB-192 RESULT, 'What could not be built'): a live page rewrites the moving cloud's status line as each 15-minute frame lands ('Computing: to H+1 h 15 min of H+6 h ...; frame 5 of 24') and draws that frame's outlines. A replay of a committed brief hands every held frame to the page in one burst before the map is drawn, so the status line mid-run is seen only in a live run with the engine in the models image; the committed screenshot of it (docs/evidence/hb192/csx_night_status_mid_run.png) is frame 5's own event replayed through the page's handler after the run. What would show it without the engine: a replay that paces the held frames at their recorded engine times (docs/evidence/hb192/frames.tsv, engine_wall_s).
